# Technician Management System — development rules

- Build in controlled phases. Do not implement the entire application in one pass.
- Inspect existing implementation before changing architecture.
- Do not rewrite working modules unnecessarily.
- Group related changes first, then verify at a checkpoint.

## Backend

- Do not run `mvn clean install` after every edit.
- Do not restart the backend after every small change.
- Run focused tests for the changed feature.
- Run a full backend build only at meaningful checkpoints (end of a phase).
- Keep controllers thin. Keep business logic in services.
- Do not expose JPA entities directly through REST. Use DTOs.
- Always enforce authorization in the backend. Do not rely on React for security.
- A technician must never access another technician's data by changing IDs in the URL.
- Do not bypass failing tests.
- Do not remove validation or security simply to make tests pass.

## Frontend

- Mobile responsiveness is mandatory, not optional.
- Technician screens are mobile-first: cards, large tap targets, no wide tables, no horizontal scroll.
